+    previous: "2026-09-11-initial"
+    after: "720f0354700d1adf1d56cd3c5d1ce708d285c770134578028a175c7141ba911f"
+    decision: same-version
+  - root: "SessionHeader"
+    previous: "2026-09-16-session-format-v4"
+    after: "b83636858c092bb763f8bc7cd561aa8d99172ea880e454b4290f4b8a273ca948"
+    decision: same-version
+```
+
+<a id="compatibility"></a>
+## Compatibility
+
+Origin-less and subagent headers retain their existing interpretation. The pinned dsh-v0.2.1-rc.5 V4 reader rejects sidechat in both header-only and streaming decode before interpreting the header, so older readers fail closed and cannot open sidechat logs until updated. The new reader preserves the origin and enforces its no-parent invariant. This supports a same-version decision without modifying the finalized V4 record.
+
+<a id="verification"></a>
+## Verification
+
+At the clean `dsh-v0.2.1-rc.5` source tag, a temporary compatibility spec ran the actual released V4 codec against a physical sidechat header; `decodeHeader` and `createDecoder` both rejected it with `released v2 header origin must be "subagent"`. Current origin roundtrip and malformed-header cases are covered by the focused V4 codec and JSONL specs.
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+## Dev Note
+
+None.
