+---
+kind: upgrade-guide
+description: "New sidechat Session headers are rejected by older Harness readers."
+---
+
+# Sidechat Session origin
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+Harness can persist an independent sidechat root with `origin: "sidechat"` in the current Session format. The pinned `dsh-v0.2.1-rc.5` reader rejects this unknown origin before opening the Session for normal use; it does not reinterpret the sidechat as a regular root or a subagent. Existing `subagent` headers and ordinary root Sessions retain their existing meaning.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. Build or install a Harness version that recognizes `SIDECHAT_SESSION_ORIGIN` before opening Sessions written by a sidechat-capable Host. Do not remove or rewrite the origin field.
+2. Rebuild the Host and Client from the same compatible source revision so both published capability checks are available.
+3. Confirm the upgrade by creating a sidechat, restarting Harness, and cold-resuming it. Existing ordinary and subagent Sessions require no conversion.
